# Context

## Background
Task T038 (tag looper:finding:pi-usage-open-fields) asked to verify the Pi
usage fields reasoning and cacheWrite against real sessions. The T037
baseline knew only the six captured T012 sessions (Pi 0.84.2 / 1.5.2,
openai-responses and one zai error), where both fields were 0.

## Verification evidence (2026-11-14)
Scanned all 74 real session files under ~/.pi/agent/sessions — 524
assistant usage records (517 zai via openai-completions, 7 anthropic via
anthropic-messages; glm-4.6/4.7/5/5.2/5.3, claude-opus-4-6/4-8):

- cacheWrite non-zero in 7 anthropic-messages records; in every one
  input + cacheRead + cacheWrite + output = totalTokens and the sum
  without cacheWrite fails -> strictly additive, not part of input.
- reasoning: no non-zero sample anywhere (key absent from all 524 real
  usage objects; 0 in the captured openai-responses records) -> stays
  unmapped.
- cacheWrite1h (new field, 3 claude-opus-4-8 records) is 0 everywhere ->
  stays unmapped.
- responseId absent on 521 of 524 records incl. 507 with non-zero usage
  (openai-completions never emits one) -> entry-id fallback needed or
  96.8% of real usage records silently counted nothing.

## End-to-end run
bin/ohya ingest --once over the real sessions root into a private hub:
524 usage rows, all four sums equal to raw-file sums (input 842,406;
cache creation 25,493; cache read 6,555,812; output 165,250), 521 rows
keyed by entry id, 3 by responseId, all rows parser_version 2; v1-stamped
copy re-derived to identical totals.

## Gotchas
- Entry ids are unique per file (verified across the corpus) and 8-hex;
  responseIds are resp_.../msg_..., so the two key spaces never collide.
- With the fallback, error responses now contribute a zero usage row
  keyed by their entry id; sums are unaffected.

